# Dockerfile-adjacent ignore-file for sidecar/docling/Dockerfile (same mechanism the
# root Dockerfile.dockerignore uses): BuildKit resolves this ahead of the root
# .dockerignore, so the docling build gets its own lean context instead of the
# SPA-tuned root one. Build context is still the repo root -- KEEP
# sidecar/docling/** and internal/platform/buildsha.txt; exclude everything else.

# Frontend / Node
node_modules
**/node_modules
frontend
packages
package.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
Caddyfile
**/dist
**/.vite
**/.verify

# Go backend + DB/migration tooling -- not part of this image
cmd
internal
!internal/platform/buildsha.txt
migrations
db
*.go
go.mod
go.sum

# VCS / CI / tooling / docs
.git
.github
.claude
backlog
docs
e2e
*.md

# Docker / env / editor / OS
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.dockerignore
.dockerignore
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
.env
.env.*
**/.env
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Local dev cruft under sidecar/docling/ itself
sidecar/docling/__pycache__
sidecar/docling/**/__pycache__
sidecar/docling/.pytest_cache
sidecar/docling/.ruff_cache
sidecar/docling/.venv
sidecar/docling/build.txt
